--TEST--
Under `[regex] backtracking = "deny"`, a `Core\Regex::compile` literal only the backtracking engine accepts does not compile, and a linear literal beside it is not reported — `rule:core-classes/regex-compile-time-tiering`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The lookbehind needs the backtracking engine, so the program never starts.
// The anchored pattern above it is linear and is not reported.
var $digits = Core\Regex::compile('^\d+$');
var $behind = Core\Regex::compile('(?<=a)X');
echo "compiled\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[regex]
backtracking = "deny"
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0893]: This pattern needs the backtracking regex engine. `[regex] backtracking` is `deny` in `nvs.toml`.
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
